<title>POLAND: SWARZEDZ FALLS IN PROFIT-TAKING.</title>
<headline>SWARZEDZ FALLS IN PROFIT-TAKING.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish furniture maker Swarzedz SA fell four percent to 9.5 zlotys in profit-taking, extending Tuesday's two-percent fall after surging 31 percent over three sessions on the news of a 200-million-mark deal, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a classic profit-taking correction,&quot; one trader said, adding that the stock could now stabilise.</p>
<p>Tuesday December 24 was the last bourse session before the Christmas break.</p>
<p>Under the deal Swarzedz will produce furniture to the year 2002 for Germany's International Moebelhandelskantor Gmbh &amp; Co, part of Schieder Group. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
